<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Del Carretto</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Del Carretto were a Ligurian and Piedmontese noble family descended from the Aleramici marquises of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/savona">Savona</a>. From the 12th century they ruled the Marquisate of Finale and other fiefs on the western Riviera, with their seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/finalborgo">Finalborgo</a>, while the port of Noli freed itself from them in 1192. Finale passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1602.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/del-carretto.jpg" alt="Del Carretto" width="320" height="372" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coat_of_arms_of_the_House_of_Del_Carretto.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
